Title: Chris Gotterup holds off Rory McIlroy to win Scottish Open
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Chris Gotterup', 'Text': 'I just hung in there tight and tried to keep it together.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 25, 'EndChar': 79}}, {'Speaker': 'Chris Gotterup', 'Text': "It's amazing. It's all hitting me. It's just so cool. I played really well this week and I knew today was going to be tough.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 109}}, {'Speaker': 'Chris Gotterup', 'Text': 'It was a pleasure to be out there with Rory and obviously all the support he gets is amazing, but it was nice to kind of ruin that a little bit.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 137}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': 'It was pretty windy and hard to get the ball super close. I gave myself plenty of chances coming down the stretch. Chris played a great round of golf. He was so solid.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 25, 'StartChar': 55, 'EndChar': 224}}, {'Speaker': 'Rory McIlroy', 'Text': "It's been a great week. I'm really happy with where my game is. No frustration, really.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 26, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 81}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'The world number 158, who began the final round tied for the lead with McIlroy, displayed admirable nerve to register a closing 66 and triumph by two shots on 15 under at the Renaissance Club.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 166}}, {'Description': "McIlroy's challenge faltered on the back nine and he shared second place with England's Marco Penge.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 93}}, {'Description': 'As well as winning £1.2m and his second PGA Tour title, 25-year-old Gotterup secured a debut appearance in The Open at Royal Portrush next week.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 124}}, {'Description': 'Matt Fitzpatrick finished three shots off the top alongside Nicolai Hojgaard, while Justin Rose was one further back after posting the lowest round of the day with a bogey-free 63.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 8, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 168}}, {'Description': 'Xander Schauffele, who begins his Claret Jug defence on Thursday, ended on nine under alongside world number one Scottie Scheffler and Ludvig Aberg.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 9, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 128}}, {'Description': "Dane Hojgaard and Germany's Matti Schmid earned the other two Open places that were available for those not already exempt.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 104}}, {'Description': 'Crowd favourite McIlroy was the star attraction in the leading group but Gotterup - in just his second competitive outing on a links course - upstaged the world number two and several other star names.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 13, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 178}}, {'Description': 'Having started shakily with a bogey, the American recovered strongly to pick up birdies on three, seven and eight.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 14, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 93}}, {'Description': 'Fitzpatrick and Penge briefly were briefly among the leaders but Gotterup and McIlroy reached the turn locked together on 13 under.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 15, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 117}}, {'Description': 'That parity did not last long as Gotterup birdied two of the ensuing three holes to seize a two-shot advantage.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 16, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 95}}, {'Description': 'His lead was halved when he overshot the 15th green and made bogey, but he immediately fought back with a 10-foot birdie on the par-five 16th where McIlroy could only post par.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 17, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 148}}, {'Description': 'The Northern Irishman failed to find a single birdie in his final 10 holes, but remained upbeat despite missing out on a second Scottish Open title in three years.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 18, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 139}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'Chris Gotterup with the Scottish Open trophy'}]}
